[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Rules model [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhich rules data model should we build?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Validator functions (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mrules = { field: [required(), minLength(3)] }, each validator (value, allValues) => message|null. Tiny engine, free
[39m     [38;5;246mcustom + cross-field rules. Not serializable.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: Plain-data schema
     [38;5;246mrules = { field: { required: true, minLength: 3 } }. Serializable and very readable, but a larger engine plus a [39m
     [38;5;246mcustom-function escape hatch, and awkward cross-field rules.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: One validate fn per form
     [38;5;246mModule ships only helper predicates; each form writes its own validate(values). Least framework, but every form [39m
     [38;5;246mre-writes the per-field loop — the duplication you asked to remove.[39m
